CM ============================================================
CM  TM-SC-NEC-010: Screwdriver Antenna — 160m Band
CM  2.4m whip, base loading coil + extension coil, 4 elevated radials
CM  Frequency: 1.800–2.000 MHz (11 points, 0.020 MHz step)
CM
CM  Loading coil (series RL at base, segment 1 of GW1):
CM  COMBINED base coil + extension coil values:
CM    R = 16.86 ohm  (total coil resistance, Q~200 at 1.8 MHz)
CM    X = 3371 ohm   (total XL required to resonate 2.4m whip on 160m)
CM
CM  Physical note: achieving X=3371 ohm at 1.8 MHz requires
CM  L = X / (2*pi*f) = 3371 / (2*pi*1.8e6) = 297.9 uH
CM  This is a very large inductance. A practical screwdriver coil
CM  (e.g., Hustler, Tarheel) may not reach full 160m resonance
CM  without an additional fixed "extension coil" in series at base.
CM  Model combines both coils as single LD for NEC-2 simplicity.
CM
CM  Whip: 2.4m, avg radius 0.006m, 20 segments
CM  Radials: 4 x 2.4m at z=0.005m, 90 deg spacing
CM  Ground: real (Sommerfeld-Norton), eps=13, sigma=0.005
CM  Feed: 1V voltage source at GW1, seg 1
CM
CM  Tuning note: 160m mobile is extremely difficult. Rrad < 0.1 ohm
CM  for a 2.4m whip; coil loss (16.86 ohm) is ~170x Rrad.
CM  System efficiency below 1% (-20 dBd or worse) is expected.
CM  Use only as reference for theoretical performance comparison.
CM  In practice, 160m screwdriver operation requires very large
CM  (18-24" dia) coil, excellent bond to vehicle body, and
CM  patience. Not recommended for portable operation.
CM  FR sweep: 1.800-2.000 MHz (US 160m band).
